The `.limit_depth()` function is called before `data->hctx` is initialized with `data->hctx = blk_mq_map_queue(q, data->cmd_flags, data->ctx);`. This means that any implementation of `.limit_depth()` may operate on an uninitialized or incorrect `hctx`, leading to undefined behavior or incorrect scheduling of I/O requests.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
data->hctx = blk_mq_map_queue(q, data->cmd_flags, data->ctx);
if (ops->limit_depth)
    ops->limit_depth(data->cmd_flags, data);
```
Reason:
The patch moves the assignment of `data->hctx` to occur before the call to `.limit_depth()`. This ensures that `data->hctx` is properly initialized before it is used in the `.limit_depth()` function, preventing any undefined behavior or incorrect scheduling of I/O requests.

